<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  socom lesson — a durable, retrievable rule earned from experience. The
  engine SOCOM only gestured at (the .socom/lessons/ stub). Ported from
  Akili's lesson system (LESSON-SYSTEM-ENGINEERING.md): a lesson is BORN
  provisional, EARNS active by re-confirmation, and is RETIRED (never
  deleted) when falsified — status indicates disposition, history is kept.

  The dominant birth path is the eval->lesson bridge: `socom cycle` surfaces
  hotspots (promises with repeated `broken` verdicts); `socom lesson
  candidates` turns each into a provisional lesson citing the cycle it came
  from. A lesson consumes the cycle's PUBLISHED hotspots (published-language),
  never the ledger internals.

  RETRIEVAL is free: this artifact lives at .socom/lessons/<id>.xml, so
  `socom index` (which rglobs .socom/**.xml) emits its embed="true" elements
  as chunks, filterable by the `domain` attribute. The lifecycle filter
  excludes state="retired" from retrieval — a retired lesson stays on disk
  and queryable for audit, but never surfaces as live guidance.

  LIFECYCLE attribute drives the deterministic retrieval map; state drives
  the live/retired filter; source records provenance (cycle|human|council).
-->
<lesson id="L-P-2026-0612-002"
        domain="data-pipeline"
        state="provisional"
        source="cycle"
        lifecycle="mid-session">

  <!-- WHAT — the rule/guard, the embedded chunk that earns retrieval. -->
  <statement embed="true">
    A failed product run must record status='failure' in dbo.run BEFORE the
    notebook re-raises — assert the insert is in the except path on every
    change to a run-recording promise.
  </statement>

  <!-- WHY — the reasoning, so the rule is applied with judgment not by rote. -->
  <why embed="true">
    The promise P-2026-0612-002 broke twice on the same contract: the failure
    path skipped run-recording, so the orchestrator saw an exception with no
    durable trace. The class is "side effects that must outlive the raise."
  </why>

  <!-- WHERE IT CAME FROM — provenance: the hotspot + cycle that birthed it.
       `derived-from` is the idempotency key: one lesson per source promise. -->
  <derived-from promise="P-2026-0612-002"
                cycle="cycle-20260613T215912+0000.json"
                broken="2" total="3"/>

  <evidence embed="true">
    cycle hotspot: P-2026-0612-002 broken 2/3; first-attempt verdict broken.
  </evidence>

  <!-- HOW SETTLED — re-confirmation counter; promote suggestion at >= 5
       (Akili threshold). active is earned, not assigned at birth. -->
  <validated count="0"/>

  <!-- On retirement: state="retired", this element set, body NEVER deleted.
       <retire reason="superseded by idempotent insert" date="2026-..."/> -->

</lesson>
